main|func() -> ():
    ; readLine keeps the line terminator, so the length includes it: the test
    ; injects "hello\n" and expects 6 rather than 5. The inherited fixture
    ; feeds newline-free input, from when the interpreter stripped it, so a
    ; stripping channel and a keeping channel print the same bytes there.
    ; Only the length is printed, never the line itself.
    print(len(readLine()))
    return
